            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0430" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-03T11:00:00-05:00">February 3, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Following for Johnson as Department’s No. 45: Your telegram February 2, midnight,
                    received. Apparently you had not then received the Department’s telegram 43,
                    January 30, 5 p.m., which authorized you in your discretion to sign the court
                    agreement. The <pb facs="0431" n="333" xml:id="pg333"/> Department is gratified
                    that you are not to be the only Minister signing this document.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
